source_1 = "record 22.30.105 [doc.07] (misleading): Lines 39-42 and 50-52 repeat router and /rpc drift; lines 198-200 list obsolete RPC surfaces; line 51 reports 18 methods instead of the site page 15."
source_2 = "record 22.30.116 [doc.05] (misleading): Read the page and checked its network, endpoint and lifecycle claims. The wiki repeats the router URL and POST /rpc, /rpc/schema and /rpc/ws endpoints, while claiming 18 methods where the site page claims 15. It conflates hosted gateway methods and public node RPC. Rewrite proposal: Regenerate or rewrite docs/wiki/HostedGateway.md from the same current OpenRPC and deployment source as the site page, documenting hosted px_ methods separately from the node root RPC and current authentication."
source_3 = "record 22.30.125 [doc.gateway_wiki] (misleading): Read full page. Lines 38-41 describe unified router and EVM-only nodes; 50-52, 198-201 and 609-611 advertise retired /rpc paths. Lines 285-300 retain legacy lx submission and network/authority language. Replace with root node JSON-RPC and hosted px OpenRPC; see gateway_wiki_router."
